    "html": "\n  <div class=\"hero-meta\">\n    <span class=\"level-badge\" data-level=\"3\">Level 3 - Intermediate</span><span class=\"time\">25 min</span>\n    <span class=\"chip warn\">Medium</span><span class=\"chip accent\">BFS</span><span class=\"chip accent\">Tree views</span>\n    <a class=\"chip\" href=\"https://leetcode.com/problems/binary-tree-vertical-order-traversal/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">LC 314</a> <span class=\"chip warn\">Premium</span>\n  </div>\n  <h1>Binary Tree Vertical Order Traversal</h1>\n  <p class=\"lead\">BFS with a column number on every queued node, append each value to its column's bucket, and track the smallest and largest column. BFS already delivers \"top to bottom, then left to right\", so no sort is needed: read the buckets from min to max. O(n) time, O(n) space.</p>\n"
